            <ArticleTitle>Potential risks in coronary artery bypass grafting via mini-thoracotomy: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>82-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This paper describes a patient with an occluded left internal thoracic artery, possibly as a result of the proximal 'steal phenomena', following coronary artery bypass grafting via mini-thoracotomy without cardiopulmonary bypass.</AbstractText>
